00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.460
<v Orlando>All right, grammar-wise, what are we talking about?

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:17.513
<v Orlando>There are certain verbs that don't take objects, and if
they don't take an object, then the word order is changed.

00:03:17.513 --> 00:03:19.550
<v Orlando>So, for example, normally you would say

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.750
<v Valdo><lang pt-BR>Maria compra as frutas.</lang>

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:26.800
<v Orlando>Mary buys the fruit. And Marcos
studies French, how would you say that?

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.650
<v Valdo><lang pt-BR>Marcos estuda francês.</lang>

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:37.601
<v Orlando>Subject, verb, object. But there's some verbs that don't take
objects. For example, there are three small dogs in the house.

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:38.750
<v Orlando>So you can't say

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:41.800
<v Orlando>three dogs exist something.

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:42.800
<v Valdo>Mm-hmm.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:46.050
<v Orlando>There exists three dogs, but you can't say three dogs existed,

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.500
<v Orlando>or three dogs exist them.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.090
<v Orlando>Those kind of verbs that don't have
objects, you put the verb first.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:04:00.470
<v Orlando>So you'd say <lang pt-BR>existem três cachorros</lang>. And so
in our dialogue, we had, there are people.

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:04.300
<v Orlando>And so instead of saying <lang pt-BR>pessoas existem</lang>, we said,

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:06.300
<v Michelle><lang pt-BR>Existem pessoas.</lang>

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:13.300
<v Orlando>Later on, instead of saying there are specific places,
we didn't say <lang pt-BR>lugares específicos têm</lang>, we said,

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:15.550
<v Valdo><lang pt-BR>Têm lugares específicos.</lang>

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:23.050
<v Orlando>And when we said there are leftover motives or the motives
that go on, instead of saying <lang pt-BR>motivos sobram</lang>, we said,

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.550
<v Valdo><lang pt-BR>Sobram motivos.</lang>

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:30.160
<v Orlando>There you go. So in all these cases, you're going to have the
verb first, and then you have the subject that comes after that.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:31.030
<v Orlando>Yes.

